60,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option B is the most logical choice. It addresses the fuel imbalance and the scheduling friction by linking payment to actual distance and requiring advance booking, ensuring a fair distribution of costs and usage.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B is mathematically precise, yet I fear it is a recipe for the very suspicion I mentioned. Tracking every kilometer risks turning our friendship into a series of audits. Perhaps Option A offers a more peaceful coexistence.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A provides the most stability for daily use. If I know the car is mine on a specific day, I can rely on its availability and ensure it is kept in a proper state.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option A is just another way to let people slide. If you don't use your day, you're still paying, but the fuel imbalance remains. Option B is the only one that actually forces honesty.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option A might be better. If we have fixed days, we wouldn't have to spend so many hours every week arguing and rearranging the schedule. It would be much quieter and simpler.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, while Option A is simpler, it doesn't solve the financial imbalance I found in the records. We cannot ignore that some are subsidizing others. Option B ensures that those who use the car more pay their fair share.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, fairness is a seductive goal, but at what cost? If we prioritize the ledger over the relationship, we may find ourselves with a perfectly balanced account and no friends left to share the ride with.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, friendship is not maintained by ignoring problems, but by solving them. Option A removes the daily stress of uncertainty. If we have fixed days, the responsibility for the car's condition also becomes clear and accountable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, accountability is a fantasy if the money is still a mess. Option A is just a lazy compromise. If we want to stop the guesswork and the subsidizing, we need the precision of Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I understand the money is important, but the stress of the scheduling is really hard for me. Option B still requires us to manage a calendar and track everything... I think Option A is the only way to truly stop the arguing.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, I understand the mental toll of scheduling, but Option A ignores the 280,000 yen fixed cost and the fuel gap. We cannot build a ""quiet"" system on a foundation of financial unfairness. Option B is the only sustainable path.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, sustainability is not merely financial; it is emotional. If we adopt Option B, we invite a culture of surveillance. I believe Option A, despite its imperfections, preserves our dignity and prevents us from becoming each other's auditors.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, financial fairness is important, but it is useless if the car is unavailable or dirty when needed. Option A creates a clear boundary of responsibility. If the car is a mess on my day, I know exactly who was responsible.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, you're obsessed with the car's condition, but you're ignoring the theft. Option A is a gift to the people who've been dodging the bills. I'm voting for B. Let's stop pretending and just be honest about the money.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm sorry, but I can't agree to Option B. Tracking every single kilometer sounds like it would just lead to more checking and arguing over figures. I really just want the stress to stop. I'll vote for Option A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minako,,"We have a clear divide between those prioritizing emotional peace and those prioritizing financial accuracy. However, a system that ignores actual costs is not fair. I will vote for Option B to ensure a truly equitable split.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are at an impasse between the ledger and the heart. To avoid the toxicity of constant auditing, I shall vote for Option A. Let us choose peace over precision.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I prioritize reliability and accountability. Option B is too administratively heavy and doesn't guarantee the car's state. Option A ensures I can depend on the vehicle's availability and condition on my days. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"It's pathetic that you're all so afraid of the truth that you'd rather keep a broken system. Fine, be ""peaceful"" while some of us keep paying for your rides. I'm voting for Option B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm sorry that we can't all agree. But for me, the mental exhaustion is too much. I really need things to be simpler so we can stop fighting. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
